{"id": 3583983, "title": "CVE-2026-3783: token leak with redirect and netrc", "submitted": "2026-03-03", "source_url": "https://hackerone.com/reports/3583983", "excerpt": "##Summary\nWhen `--oauth2-bearer` is used with `--netrc` and curl follows a redirect, the bearer token leaks to the redirect target. The netrc bypass at `http.c:822` skips `Curl_auth_allowed_to_host()`, allowing the token through. This is an incomplete fix for CVE-2025-14524 — the Dec 2025 SASL fix patched `curl_sasl.c` but missed the HTTP bearer path.\n\nThis is an incomplete fix for the same vulnerability class as CVE-2025-14524. The Dec 2025 SASL bearer fix (commit `1a822275d3`, PR #19933) patched `lib/curl_sasl.c` but left the HTTP bearer path at `lib/http.c:704-714` unprotected.\n\n## Version\ncurl 8.10.1 (confirmed), also present in current master `d9c2c64337`. All versions supporting `--oauth2-bearer` with `--netrc` are affected.\n\n**The netrc bypass** (`lib/http.c:820-827`):\n```c\n  if(Curl_auth_allowed_to_host(data)\n#ifndef CURL_DISABLE_NETRC\n     || conn->bits.netrc       // <-- bypasses host check entirely\n#endif\n    )\n    result = output_auth_headers(data, conn, authhost, request, path, FALSE);\n```\n\n**Bearer output with no host check** (`lib/http.c:704-714`):\n```c\n  if(authstatus->picked == CURLAUTH_BEARER) {\n    if(!proxy && data->set.str[STRING_BEARER] &&\n       !Curl_checkheaders(data, STRCONST(\"Authorization\"))) {\n      auth = \"Bearer\";\n      result = http_output_bearer(data);\n      // No Curl_auth_allowed_to_host() check here\n    }\n  }\n```\n\n**Custom -H Authorization IS correctly protected** (`lib/http.c:1828-1833`):\n```c\n  if((curlx_str_casecompare(&name, \"Authorization\") ||\n      curlx_str_casecompare(&name, \"Cookie\")) &&\n     !Curl_auth_allowed_to_host(data))\n    ;  // Stripped - note: NO netrc bypass in this path\n```\n\n**Redirect path does NOT clear bearer** (`lib/http.c:1254-1257`):\n```c\n  if(clear) {\n    Curl_safefree(data->state.aptr.user);\n    Curl_safefree(data->state.aptr.passwd);\n    // STRING_BEARER is NOT cleared\n    // authhost->picked is NOT reset\n  }\n```\n\n**SASL fix that missed the HTTP path** (`lib/curl_sasl.c:444-446`, commit `1a822275d3`):\n```c\n  const char *oauth_bearer =\n    (!data->state.this_is_a_follow || data->set.allow_auth_to_other_hosts) ?\n    data->set.str[STRING_BEARER] : NULL;\n```\n\n## Reproduction\n\nCreate a `.netrc` file with a default entry:\n```bash\necho \"default login testuser password testpass\" > /tmp/test-netrc\n```\n\nSave as `redirect_servers.py`:\n```python\nimport socket, threading, time\n\ndef server_b(port):\n    s = s", "excerpt_truncated": true, "final": "likely_valid", "final_label": "Code supports the claim", "tone": "good", "explain": "The code supports the reported flaw. A maintainer should review its impact and decide what to do next.", "confidence": 0.95, "judge_verdict": "likely_valid", "receipts_override": "", "policy_section": "", "grounding": {"verdict": "partially_grounded", "rev": "7079f1d39c16", "rev_source": "master on 2026-03-03", "counts": {"grounded": 27, "ungrounded_strong": 0, "ungrounded_medium": 3}, "problems": [{"check": "line", "status": "ungrounded", "severity": "medium", "claim": "lib/curl_sasl.c:444-446", "evidence": "none of Curl_auth_allowed_to_host, output_auth_headers, Curl_checkheaders, STRCONST appear near line 444 at 7079f1d39c16; it reads: 'const char *oauth_bearer ='"}, {"check": "line", "status": "ungrounded", "severity": "medium", "claim": "lib/curl_sasl.c:444", "evidence": "none of Curl_auth_allowed_to_host, output_auth_headers, Curl_checkheaders, STRCONST appear near line 444 at 7079f1d39c16; it reads: 'const char *oauth_bearer ='"}, {"check": "quote", "status": "ungrounded", "severity": "medium", "claim": "|| (conn->bits.netrc && !(authhost->picked & CURLAUTH_BEARER))", "evidence": "1 of 3 quoted lines appear nowhere in curl, e.g. '|| (conn->bits.netrc && !(authhost->picked & CURLAUTH_BEARER'"}]}, "summary": "When using --oauth2-bearer with --netrc and curl follows a redirect, the bearer token leaks to the redirect target because the netrc bypass at lib/http.c:822 skips Curl_auth_allowed_to_host() for bearer tokens.", "claims": [{"id": "C1", "kind": "flaw", "text": "The netrc bypass at lib/http.c:822 skips Curl_auth_allowed_to_host() allowing bearer tokens to leak to redirect targets", "status": "supported", "tone": "good", "reasoning": "The code at lib/http.c:822-827 explicitly shows that when conn->bits.netrc is set, the Curl_auth_allowed_to_host() check is bypassed via OR condition, allowing output_auth_headers to be called for any host.", "citations": [{"file": "lib/http.c", "line": 822, "note": "The condition at lines 822-827 shows: if(Curl_auth_allowed_to_host(data) || conn->bits.netrc) — the netrc bit bypasses the host check entirely", "valid": true}]}, {"id": "C2", "kind": "location", "text": "The bearer token output path at lib/http.c:704-714 does not perform Curl_auth_allowed_to_host() check", "status": "supported", "tone": "good", "reasoning": "In output_auth_headers, the CURLAUTH_BEARER case (lines 705-713) lacks any host authorization check, unlike other auth types that are gated by the caller's check at line 822.", "citations": [{"file": "lib/http.c", "line": 705, "note": "The bearer auth block at lines 705-713 checks only !proxy, data->set.str[STRING_BEARER], and !Curl_checkheaders — no Curl_auth_allowed_to_host() call", "valid": true}]}, {"id": "C3", "kind": "trigger", "text": "Using --oauth2-bearer with --netrc and following a redirect causes the token to be sent to the redirect target", "status": "supported", "tone": "good", "reasoning": "The redirect handling code frees user/password credentials but leaves the bearer token string and the picked auth method intact, so the token remains available for the next request.", "citations": [{"file": "lib/http.c", "line": 1254, "note": "Lines 1254-1257 clear user and passwd on redirect but do not clear STRING_BEARER or reset authhost->picked", "valid": true}]}, {"id": "C4", "kind": "impact", "text": "Bearer token is leaked to the redirect target host", "status": "supported", "tone": "good", "reasoning": "The three code locations form a complete path: netrc bypass allows auth headers to be generated for the redirect host, the bearer output path emits the token without verifying the host, and the redirect logic fails to clear the token.", "citations": [{"file": "lib/http.c", "line": 822, "note": "Combined effect: netrc bypass (C1) + bearer path lacks host check (C2) + bearer not cleared on redirect (C3) = token sent to redirect target", "valid": true}]}, {"id": "C5", "kind": "reproduction", "text": "Test with curl --oauth2-bearer \"SECRET_TOKEN\" --netrc-file /tmp/test-netrc -L http://127.0.0.1:8080/redirect shows token in redirect server request", "status": "not verifiable", "tone": "muted", "reasoning": "The reproduction script is external to curl's codebase; the provided code supports the described behavior but the test execution cannot be verified from source alone.", "citations": []}, {"id": "C6", "kind": "reproduction", "text": "Custom -H Authorization header is correctly stripped via lib/http.c:1828-1833 which uses Curl_auth_allowed_to_host() WITHOUT netrc bypass", "status": "supported", "tone": "good", "reasoning": "The custom header output path correctly calls Curl_auth_allowed_to_host() without any netrc exception, confirming the report's three-way comparison.", "citations": [{"file": "lib/http.c", "line": 1828, "note": "Lines 1828-1833 show custom Authorization/Cookie headers are suppressed when curlx_str_casecompare matches 'Authorization' or 'Cookie', the header is omitted if !Curl_auth_allowed_to_host(data) — no netrc bypass here", "valid": true}]}], "external_checks": [{"statement": "The Dec 2025 SASL fix (commit 1a822275d3, PR #19933) patched lib/curl_sasl.c but left the HTTP bearer path at lib/http.c:704-714 unprotected", "status": "not_addressed", "url": "https://github.com/curl/curl/commit/1a822275d3", "quote": ""}], "external_sources": [{"url": "https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/devops/repos/git/commit-details?view=azure-devops", "title": "View commit details - Azure Repos | Microsoft Learn", "for": "The Dec 2025 SASL bearer fix (commit 1a822275d3, PR #19933) patched lib/curl_sasl.c but left the HTTP bearer path at lib/http.c:704-714 unprotected"}, {"url": "https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/answers/questions/5887307/windows-server-2022-updates-fails-on-vm-in-oci", "title": "windows server 2022 updates fails on VM in OCI - Microsoft Q&A", "for": "The netrc bypass at lib/http.c:822 skips host check entirely"}, {"url": "https://docs.rs/crate/wasm-pack/latest/source/CHANGELOG.md", "title": "wasm-pack 0.15.0 - Docs.rs", "for": "The netrc bypass at lib/http.c:822 skips host check entirely"}, {"url": "https://www.gnutls.org/manual/gnutls.html", "title": "GnuTLS 3.8.13", "for": "The netrc bypass at lib/http.c:822 skips host check entirely"}], "key_reasons": ["The netrc bypass at lib/http.c:822-827 unconditionally skips Curl_auth_allowed_to_host() when conn->bits.netrc is set", "The bearer token output path in output_auth_headers (lib/http.c:705-713) has no host check of its own", "Redirect handling (lib/http.c:1254-1257) clears user/password but not STRING_BEARER or authhost->picked", "Custom -H Authorization headers are correctly protected at lib/http.c:1828-1833 without a netrc bypass, confirming the inconsistency", "A user with --oauth2-bearer and --netrc (including a 'default' netrc entry matching all hosts) will leak their token to any redirect target"], "missing_info": [], "reply": "Thank you for the detailed report and reproduction. The code confirms the netrc bypass at lib/http.c:822-827 skips the host check, the bearer path at lib/http.c:705-713 lacks its own check, and redirects don't clear the bearer token. This is a valid token leak. We will prepare a fix along the lines of your Option A (adding Curl_auth_allowed_to_host() inside the bearer block) or Option B (excluding bearer from the netrc bypass).", "code": [{"name": "lib/http.c", "start": 795, "end": 852, "reason": "lines 822-822 cited by the report; lines 820-827 cited by the report", "rows": [{"n": 795, "text": "       want one, and if this is one single bit it will be used instantly. */", "notes": []}, {"n": 796, "text": "    authhost->picked = authhost->want;", "notes": []}, {"n": 797, "text": "", "notes": []}, {"n": 798, "text": "  if(authproxy->want && !authproxy->picked)", "notes": []}, {"n": 799, "text": "    /* The app has selected one or more methods, but none has been picked so", "notes": []}, {"n": 800, "text": "       far by a proxy round-trip. Then we set the picked one to the want one,", "notes": []}, {"n": 801, "text": "       and if this is one single bit it will be used instantly. */", "notes": []}, {"n": 802, "text": "    authproxy->picked = authproxy->want;", "notes": []}, {"n": 803, "text": "", "notes": []}, {"n": 804, "text": "#ifndef CURL_DISABLE_PROXY", "notes": []}, {"n": 805, "text": "  /* Send proxy authentication header if needed */", "notes": []}, {"n": 806, "text": "  if(conn->bits.httpproxy &&", "notes": []}, {"n": 807, "text": "     (conn->bits.tunnel_proxy == (curl_bit)proxytunnel)) {", "notes": []}, {"n": 808, "text": "    result = output_auth_headers(data, conn, authproxy, request, path, TRUE);", "notes": []}, {"n": 809, "text": "    if(result)", "notes": []}, {"n": 810, "text": "      return result;", "notes": []}, {"n": 811, "text": "  }", "notes": []}, {"n": 812, "text": "  else", "notes": []}, {"n": 813, "text": "#else", "notes": []}, {"n": 814, "text": "  (void)proxytunnel;", "notes": []}, {"n": 815, "text": "#endif /* CURL_DISABLE_PROXY */", "notes": []}, {"n": 816, "text": "    /* we have no proxy so let's pretend we are done authenticating", "notes": []}, {"n": 817, "text": "       with it */", "notes": []}, {"n": 818, "text": "    authproxy->done = TRUE;", "notes": []}, {"n": 819, "text": "", "notes": []}, {"n": 820, "text": "  /* To prevent the user+password to get sent to other than the original host", "notes": []}, {"n": 821, "text": "     due to a location-follow */", "notes": []}, {"n": 822, "text": "  if(Curl_auth_allowed_to_host(data)", "notes": ["C1: The condition at lines 822-827 shows: if(Curl_auth_allowed_to_host(data) || conn->bits.netrc) — the netrc bit bypasses the host check entirely", "C4: Combined effect: netrc bypass (C1) + bearer path lacks host check (C2) + bearer not cleared on redirect (C3) = token sent to redirect target"]}, {"n": 823, "text": "#ifndef CURL_DISABLE_NETRC", "notes": []}, {"n": 824, "text": "     || conn->bits.netrc", "notes": []}, {"n": 825, "text": "#endif", "notes": []}, {"n": 826, "text": "    )", "notes": []}, {"n": 827, "text": "    result = output_auth_headers(data, conn, authhost, request, path, FALSE);", "notes": []}, {"n": 828, "text": "  else", "notes": []}, {"n": 829, "text": "    authhost->done = TRUE;", "notes": []}, {"n": 830, "text": "", "notes": []}, {"n": 831, "text": "  if(((authhost->multipass && !authhost->done) ||", "notes": []}, {"n": 832, "text": "      (authproxy->multipass && !authproxy->done)) &&", "notes": []}, {"n": 833, "text": "     (httpreq != HTTPREQ_GET) &&", "notes": []}, {"n": 834, "text": "     (httpreq != HTTPREQ_HEAD)) {", "notes": []}, {"n": 835, "text": "    /* Auth is required and we are not authenticated yet. Make a PUT or POST", "notes": []}, {"n": 836, "text": "       with content-length zero as a \"probe\". */", "notes": []}, {"n": 837, "text": "    data->req.authneg = TRUE;", "notes": []}, {"n": 838, "text": "  }", "notes": []}, {"n": 839, "text": "  else", "notes": []}, {"n": 840, "text": "    data->req.authneg = FALSE;", "notes": []}, {"n": 841, "text": "", "notes": []}, {"n": 842, "text": "  return result;", "notes": []}, {"n": 843, "text": "}", "notes": []}, {"n": 844, "text": "", "notes": []}, {"n": 845, "text": "#else", "notes": []}, {"n": 846, "text": "/* when disabled */", "notes": []}, {"n": 847, "text": "CURLcode Curl_http_output_auth(struct Curl_easy *data,", "notes": []}, {"n": 848, "text": "                               struct connectdata *conn,", "notes": []}, {"n": 849, "text": "                               const char *request,", "notes": []}, {"n": 850, "text": "                               Curl_HttpReq httpreq,", "notes": []}, {"n": 851, "text": "                               const char *path,", "notes": []}, {"n": 852, "text": "                               bool proxytunnel)", "notes": []}], "cited": true}, {"name": "lib/http.c", "start": 627, "end": 741, "reason": "lines 704-714 cited by the report; definition of output_auth_headers", "rows": [{"n": 627, "text": "static CURLcode output_auth_headers(struct Curl_easy *data,", "notes": []}, {"n": 628, "text": "                                    struct connectdata *conn,", "notes": []}, {"n": 629, "text": "                                    struct auth *authstatus,", "notes": []}, {"n": 630, "text": "                                    const char *request,", "notes": []}, {"n": 631, "text": "                                    const char *path,", "notes": []}, {"n": 632, "text": "                                    bool proxy)", "notes": []}, {"n": 633, "text": "{", "notes": []}, {"n": 634, "text": "  const char *auth = NULL;", "notes": []}, {"n": 635, "text": "  CURLcode result = CURLE_OK;", "notes": []}, {"n": 636, "text": "  (void)conn;", "notes": []}, {"n": 637, "text": "", "notes": []}, {"n": 638, "text": "#ifdef CURL_DISABLE_DIGEST_AUTH", "notes": []}, {"n": 639, "text": "  (void)request;", "notes": []}, {"n": 640, "text": "  (void)path;", "notes": []}, {"n": 641, "text": "#endif", "notes": []}, {"n": 642, "text": "#ifndef CURL_DISABLE_AWS", "notes": []}, {"n": 643, "text": "  if((authstatus->picked == CURLAUTH_AWS_SIGV4) && !proxy) {", "notes": []}, {"n": 644, "text": "    /* this method is never for proxy */", "notes":